I was hanging out with the cool kids in rec.games.roguelike.nethack when 
Ilmari Karonen got out a spraycan and scrawled the following:
>  There's an ascension run trick that involves tossing the amulet to a
>  covetous monster and letting him carry it for you.  It works with any
>  demon lord, but Asmodeus is the most convenient one since he's about
>  the most harmless of them all.  Since you don't really _need_ to kill
>  him, that could be a good reason to leave him alive (and unbribed).
> 
>  It does work: I just tried it in wizmode.  It does take a bit of skill
>  (and preferably a stethoscope), since you need to beat him down to one
>  third of his hit points to make him escape upstairs while making sure
>  he stays alive.  (Don't use your main weapon -- hit him with a very
>  dull knife or something instead.  But do it only _after_ he's got the
>  amulet, since he won't pick it up if his HPs are low even if you toss
>  it at him(!).)

Another option, that I just tested in wizard mode, is to use Juiblex.
It won't pick up the Amulet, but it will pick up *you*.  If you do
enough damage while remaining engulfed, it will (after a few turns;
Juiblex is very slow) take you to the upstairs - regardless of the
no-teleport status of the level - so you can effectively ride all the
way up.

Exploiting this is not especially easy.  Juiblex is very slow, so you'll
be waiting around for a several turns between actions.  You need to stop
being engulfed (preferably with the /oDig trick) to climb the stairs,
which also means that you remain vulnerable to the mysterious force.
The /oDig takes J down to 1HP, so it has to heal again (and you have to
be careful not to hit it) before it'll come back and give you the next
part of the ride.  And the sickness attack also takes off several HP, so
you need potions of healing instead of (or in addition to) your reusable
method of curing sickness - at a rate of at least two per level.

So the net result is that it's slow and not especially stylish (the
second makes it less suitable for a SAT, IMHO).  And I've no idea
whether it'll work outside of wizmode, either.

